    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The most important technique in mansaf is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "stabilising-yoghurt"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "stabilising the yoghurt"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " before heating it. Without this step the yoghurt will split and curdle into grainy lumps in the sauce. The lamb is cooked separately in a spiced broth, and the rice is fried in "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "ghee"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "ghee"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " or butter before steaming."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: use full-fat yoghurt. Low-fat yoghurt is more prone to splitting even when stabilised."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
